2. Trained weights: research use only
-------------------------------------
The MIT License does NOT extend to trained model weights. This covers every checkpoint and exported
graph, including:

  results_r2/runs/r7_e256_wr64/best.pt           (r7 backbone)
  results_r2/runs/r7_e256_wr64_refiner/best.pt   (r7 cascade refiner)
  deploy/r7/cascade.onnx                          (r7 shipping graph)
  deploy/model.onnx, deploy/tier46/, and every other results_r2/runs/*/best.pt

The weights are derived from the training corpora below, several of which carry non-commercial or
unresolved redistribution terms. They are provided for research and evaluation only, and any use is
bound by the most restrictive licence among those corpora. A fielded or commercial system must be
retrained on licensed or government-collected data; a recipe is a list of manifest paths, so the
substitution needs no code change.

Training corpora of the shipping r7 recipe (configs/retraining/r7_e256_wr64.yaml, data.manifests;
the r7 refiner inherits the backbone's data). Generated table: docs/licences.md.

  corpus      manifest                                                     licence as recorded       commercial
  librispeech data/manifests/librispeech_100h.parquet                      CC BY 4.0                 yes
  ears        data/manifests/ears.parquet                                  CC BY-NC 4.0              no
  cv_hi       data/manifests/cv_hi.parquet                                 CC0                       yes
  esc50       data/manifests/esc50.parquet                                 CC BY-NC (per clip)       no
  dns_noise   data/manifests/dns_datasets_fullband.noise_fullband.         per clip, see DNS README  unclear
              freesound_000.tar.parquet
  mad         data/manifests/mad.parquet                                   YouTube-sourced           no
  gunshots    data/manifests/gunshots.parquet                              CC BY 4.0                 yes
  drone       data/manifests/drone.parquet                                 DroneAudioDataset,        unclear
                                                                           cite Al-Emadi et al. 2019
  noisex92    data/manifests/noisex92.parquet                              NOISEX-92 via SPIB,       unclear
                                                                           terms unstated

Room impulse responses are simulated in-repo with pyroomacoustics (vaani/data/rirs.py,
data/rirs/bank_r3.npz); no recorded third-party RIRs enter the r7 recipe.

The r7 backbone was initialised from results of the r6_e256 recipe (init_from runs/r6_e256/best.pt),
which reads the same manifest list.

This is a licence statement, not a legal opinion. "unclear" means unresolved, not cleared.

